00:31:49.243 --> 00:31:50.612
[Anthony] That shit is
what I'm talking about.

514
00:31:50.645 --> 00:31:52.312
[DJ] Legit!

515
00:31:52.346 --> 00:31:54.214
You're not hungry there, Sean?

516
00:31:55.215 --> 00:31:57.050
What?

517
00:31:57.084 --> 00:31:58.352
Your food.

518
00:31:58.385 --> 00:32:00.187
You haven't touched it.

519
00:32:00.220 --> 00:32:01.589
Is something wrong?

520
00:32:01.623 --> 00:32:03.290
[Anthony] No, no, no,
my boy's fine.

521
00:32:03.323 --> 00:32:05.259
He's just tired
from the long drive up here.

522
00:32:05.292 --> 00:32:06.427
But he'll snap the fuck
out of it.

523
00:32:06.460 --> 00:32:07.261
Right, Sean?

524
00:32:07.294 --> 00:32:09.496
We don't wanna be rude
to our host.

525
00:32:11.432 --> 00:32:12.600
Yeah.

526
00:32:12.634 --> 00:32:14.569
Yeah. Sorry, sir.

527
00:32:14.602 --> 00:32:18.338
Why don't you take your hat off
at the dinner table, yeah?

528
00:32:21.008 --> 00:32:22.242
Sorry, sir.

529
00:32:23.343 --> 00:32:25.412
You boys can take it easy
on the "sir" stuff.

530
00:32:25.446 --> 00:32:28.482
I'm just a Noble Man,
same as you.

531
00:32:30.050 --> 00:32:31.485
(dog whimpering)

532
00:32:32.520 --> 00:32:34.221
It's all right, buddy.

533
00:32:43.531 --> 00:32:45.199
Why does he have
to stay in this thing?

534
00:32:45.232 --> 00:32:48.402
Oh yeah, he just hasn't been
feeling like himself lately.

535
00:32:48.435 --> 00:32:49.604
Got in a fight
with another dog

536
00:32:49.637 --> 00:32:51.205
who fucked him up pretty good.

537
00:32:51.238 --> 00:32:53.575
I just don't want him
to get all worked up.

538
00:32:53.608 --> 00:32:56.578
Yeah. Or eat us.

539
00:32:56.611 --> 00:32:59.379
It's good you're
taking care of him.

540
00:32:59.413 --> 00:33:01.081
[Twig] Hey, maybe we can
get one of our flags

541
00:33:01.114 --> 00:33:02.349
with his face on it

542
00:33:02.382 --> 00:33:04.485
and it could say,
"Noble Dog."

543
00:33:04.519 --> 00:33:07.187
No, wait, even better:
"Noble Mutt."

544
00:33:07.221 --> 00:33:08.756
(all laughing)

545
00:33:09.724 --> 00:33:11.191
[Twig] Hey, you hear that, boy?

546
00:33:11.225 --> 00:33:12.694
You're Noble Mutt.

547
00:33:14.161 --> 00:33:17.030
Yeah, that's one lucky dog
to have found us.

548
00:33:20.167 --> 00:33:21.335
Excuse me.

549
00:33:29.844 --> 00:33:32.747
Motion sickness
from the ride.

550
00:33:34.782 --> 00:33:36.518
(retching)

551
00:33:40.487 --> 00:33:42.690
(tense music)
(birds chirping)

552
00:33:59.106 --> 00:34:00.808
(window creaking)

553
00:34:01.876 --> 00:34:04.579
(tense music continues)

554
00:34:36.410 --> 00:34:38.513
(music intensifies)

555
00:35:00.434 --> 00:35:02.302
[Darryl] You feelin' okay, kid?

556
00:35:02.336 --> 00:35:04.338
(tense music)

557
00:35:05.472 --> 00:35:08.743
Yeah, good, I just
had to take a piss.

558
00:35:11.846 --> 00:35:13.380
Come with me.

559
00:35:14.247 --> 00:35:15.883
Yeah, okay.

560
00:35:20.722 --> 00:35:22.624
[Darryl] It's just up here
on your left.

561
00:35:29.329 --> 00:35:31.131
Go in there.

562
00:35:32.667 --> 00:35:34.368
You'll have to excuse the mess.

563
00:35:34.401 --> 00:35:35.335
As you can imagine,

564
00:35:35.369 --> 00:35:37.204
things have been
a little hectic around here.

565
00:35:37.772 --> 00:35:39.406
Go on, have a seat.

566
00:35:40.642 --> 00:35:46.213
So...when did you decide
to become a Noble Man?

567
00:35:46.246 --> 00:35:49.684
Um, few months back now?

568
00:35:49.717 --> 00:35:51.418
I mean, I've always
believed in the cause,

569
00:35:51.451 --> 00:35:53.186
I just didn't go
to my first rally

570
00:35:53.220 --> 00:35:54.656
until a few months ago.

571
00:35:54.689 --> 00:35:55.957
Wow.

572
00:35:55.990 --> 00:36:00.227
I would kill to experience
my first rally again.

573
00:36:00.260 --> 00:36:02.462
Anthony says
that's where you three met.

574
00:36:02.496 --> 00:36:05.900
Yeah. There was a march
back in our hometown.

575
00:36:05.933 --> 00:36:09.202
They, uh pepper-sprayed
the shit out of us.

576
00:36:09.236 --> 00:36:11.506
[Darryl] Well, it's good that
you were there to represent.

577
00:36:11.539 --> 00:36:13.541
It's important that
we show them our numbers.

578
00:36:13.574 --> 00:36:15.375
Have our voices heard,
you know?

579
00:36:15.409 --> 00:36:16.611
[Sean] Yeah, for sure.

580
00:36:18.846 --> 00:36:21.281
You wanna see
something cool?

581
00:36:21.314 --> 00:36:24.384
Uh, yep, okay.

582
00:36:24.418 --> 00:36:25.920
(tense music)

583
00:36:29.991 --> 00:36:32.259
Thumb drive.

584
00:36:32.292 --> 00:36:34.428
Not just any thumb drive.

585
00:36:34.461 --> 00:36:35.630
It's the only one of its kind

586
00:36:35.663 --> 00:36:39.199
entrusted by our founder
to yours truly.

587
00:36:40.735 --> 00:36:42.704
This is an air-gapped computer,

588
00:36:42.737 --> 00:36:43.838
our little way
to tell Uncle Sam

589
00:36:43.871 --> 00:36:46.406
to stay the fuck
out of our business.

590
00:36:49.010 --> 00:36:51.546
The 12 Disciples?

591
00:36:53.548 --> 00:36:54.782
Whoa.

592
00:36:54.816 --> 00:36:57.685
-Is that...
-It's impressive, isn't it?

593
00:36:59.352 --> 00:37:01.923
I didn't realize
how many of us there were.

594
00:37:01.956 --> 00:37:04.592
A lot more than twelve.

595
00:37:04.625 --> 00:37:05.860
[Sean] Yeah.

596
00:37:10.798 --> 00:37:13.333
Did you know
that I served overseas?

597
00:37:14.869 --> 00:37:15.937
Uh, yeah.

598
00:37:15.970 --> 00:37:20.041
DJ'd mentioned something
about you being an ex-SEAL.

599
00:37:20.074 --> 00:37:22.543
Army Ranger,
staff sergeant.

600
00:37:22.577 --> 00:37:24.344
[Darryl] Did three
tours in Iraq.

601
00:37:24.377 --> 00:37:26.581
[Sean] Wow.
[Darryl] Yeah.

602
00:37:26.614 --> 00:37:29.316
Me and my men, we, uh...

603
00:37:29.349 --> 00:37:30.518
we were in charge
of hunting down

604
00:37:30.551 --> 00:37:33.588
some of the real bad guys
over there.

605
00:37:33.621 --> 00:37:37.625
Well, um...
thank you for your service.

606
00:37:39.861 --> 00:37:43.296
You know, there was
this one night over there.

607
00:37:43.330 --> 00:37:45.800
My squad and I were
in this town

608
00:37:45.833 --> 00:37:49.570
and we were looking for this
real piece-of-shit towelhead.

609
00:37:49.604 --> 00:37:51.506
This fuckin' guy had
killed, like, fifteen of us

610
00:37:51.539 --> 00:37:53.641
at this point in the war.

611
00:37:53.674 --> 00:37:55.375
We get to his house.

612
00:37:55.408 --> 00:38:00.313
He's not there, but, uh,
his wife was.

613
00:38:00.347 --> 00:38:03.350
So, I put one of my men
out on lookout.

614
00:38:03.383 --> 00:38:04.986
This sweet kid...

615
00:38:05.019 --> 00:38:06.721
We called him Tootsie

616
00:38:06.754 --> 00:38:08.089
because he was always
having his family ship out

617
00:38:08.122 --> 00:38:10.725
those canisters
of Tootsie Rolls, right?

618
00:38:11.559 --> 00:38:15.596
Anyways, I'm, uh,
takin' my time with the wife

619
00:38:15.630 --> 00:38:17.064
and all of a sudden,
shots ring out.

620
00:38:17.098 --> 00:38:19.634
Within seconds,
all hell breaks loose.

621
00:38:19.667 --> 00:38:21.702
Bullets are just flying
in every direction.

622
00:38:21.736 --> 00:38:23.370
Tootsie bursts inside.

623
00:38:23.403 --> 00:38:25.039
He's bleeding
all over the place.

624
00:38:25.072 --> 00:38:27.642
Shot once in the shoulder,
twice in the legs.

625
00:38:27.675 --> 00:38:30.410
Shots weren't fatal
but he could hardly walk.

626
00:38:30.443 --> 00:38:31.946
Eventually, you know,
the three of us,

627
00:38:31.979 --> 00:38:34.615
we take cover
in this empty house.

628
00:38:34.649 --> 00:38:36.684
Now, we don't have a radio.

629
00:38:36.717 --> 00:38:38.085
I tell them, I said,

630
00:38:38.119 --> 00:38:41.522
"You know, our guys are
gonna come look for us."

631
00:38:41.556 --> 00:38:46.894
But Tootsie, he, uh...
couldn't keep quiet.

632
00:38:46.928 --> 00:38:48.830
He's just screaming in pain.

633
00:38:48.863 --> 00:38:52.667
Lopez and I--
that's the other guy--

634
00:38:52.700 --> 00:38:56.604
we just kept telling him,
"Shut the fuck up," you know?

635
00:38:56.637 --> 00:38:58.506
"They're gonna hear you
and they'll find us,"

636
00:38:58.539 --> 00:39:02.944
but he just
wouldn't stay calm, so...

637
00:39:05.012 --> 00:39:07.748
I took my hands

638
00:39:08.850 --> 00:39:11.619
and I put them over his face

639
00:39:12.452 --> 00:39:14.722
and I started to squeeze.

640
00:39:16.524 --> 00:39:18.391
I couldn't stop.

641
00:39:19.794 --> 00:39:23.898
Softer at first, and then,
I started to squeeze harder

642
00:39:23.931 --> 00:39:27.467
and harder, until...

643
00:39:36.978 --> 00:39:40.781
Of course, you know,
Lopez never told a soul.

644
00:39:40.815 --> 00:39:45.452
He knew that what I did was
the best thing for the squad.

645
00:39:45.485 --> 00:39:47.088
You see, that's the thing
about being part of something

646
00:39:47.121 --> 00:39:48.723
bigger than yourself.

647
00:39:48.756 --> 00:39:50.691
It's a team effort,

648
00:39:50.725 --> 00:39:53.694
and each individual on that team
has to do their part

649
00:39:53.728 --> 00:39:56.063
or they take the others down
with 'em.

650
00:39:57.231 --> 00:40:01.468
One weak link
and the entire team fails.

651
00:40:06.540 --> 00:40:08.843
You're not a weak link,
are you?

652
00:40:11.045 --> 00:40:12.613
No, sir.

653
00:40:13.547 --> 00:40:15.482
You sure about that?

654
00:40:15.950 --> 00:40:17.752
Y-yes, sir.

655
00:40:19.053 --> 00:40:22.123
And what did I say
about you boys calling me "sir"?

656
00:40:23.057 --> 00:40:24.457
Sorry.

657
00:40:30.131 --> 00:40:33.167
I am proud to be in
the brotherhood with you, buddy.

658
00:40:36.003 --> 00:40:38.005
Yeah, for sure.

659
00:40:41.108 --> 00:40:42.610
I'm just gonna...

660
00:40:45.012 --> 00:40:46.514
Hey, Sean,
one more thing.

661
00:40:46.547 --> 00:40:47.915
Yeah?

662
00:40:47.949 --> 00:40:49.817
What happened to you guys
last night?

663
00:40:49.850 --> 00:40:51.986
I was expecting you
around midnight.

664
00:40:52.019 --> 00:40:53.988
Everything go okay
on the drive?

665
00:40:54.021 --> 00:40:56.691
Yeah, we, uh,
just had a flat tire,

666
00:40:56.724 --> 00:40:59.160
decided to kill some time
at a diner.

667
00:41:00.027 --> 00:41:00.962
(sighs)

668
00:41:00.995 --> 00:41:03.798
Yeah, I figured it was
something like that.

669
00:41:04.832 --> 00:41:06.567
Go on, go on.

670
00:41:06.600 --> 00:41:07.969
Enjoy yourself.

671
00:41:10.237 --> 00:41:12.506
(footsteps receding)

672
00:41:14.241 --> 00:41:16.677
(soft music)

673
00:41:31.559 --> 00:41:33.127
(window closes)

674
00:41:45.339 --> 00:41:46.907
[Twig] Darryl!

675
00:41:46.941 --> 00:41:48.776
What the hell you doin'
in there?

676
00:41:48.809 --> 00:41:51.112
Yeah, I'm comin'.

677
00:41:53.914 --> 00:41:56.617
(footsteps receding)

678
00:42:05.893 --> 00:42:08.195
(dramatic music)

679
00:42:17.038 --> 00:42:18.672
[Becky] <i>It was right</i>
<i>then and there,</i>

680
00:42:18.706 --> 00:42:20.307
<i>scrolling through</i>
<i>that never-ending list</i>

681
00:42:20.341 --> 00:42:22.343
<i>of pencil-dick motherfuckers,</i>

682
00:42:22.376 --> 00:42:24.912
<i>that I realized</i>
<i>Elena was right.</i>

683
00:42:24.945 --> 00:42:27.048
<i>The world had gone mad.</i>

684
00:42:27.081 --> 00:42:29.350
<i>And maybe</i>
<i>I couldn't save the world</i>

685
00:42:29.383 --> 00:42:32.119
<i>but I could kill</i>
<i>some of those shit stains</i>

686
00:42:32.153 --> 00:42:35.322
<i>and I could have a whole</i>
<i>hell of a lot of fun doin' it.</i>

687
00:42:35.356 --> 00:42:38.225
(music intensifies)

688
00:43:19.433 --> 00:43:21.268
(doors opening)

689
00:43:29.910 --> 00:43:31.979
(music intensifies)

690
00:43:44.425 --> 00:43:45.993
To saving our country

691
00:43:46.026 --> 00:43:47.161
and to stopping the treason

692
00:43:47.194 --> 00:43:49.964
one vengeful mission
at a time.

693
00:43:49.997 --> 00:43:51.799
To freedom.

694
00:43:51.832 --> 00:43:53.367
-Freedom.
-Freedom.

695
00:43:54.135 --> 00:43:56.403
(door bell ringing)

696
00:43:56.437 --> 00:43:58.439
Thought she wasn't comin'
till tonight.

697
00:43:58.472 --> 00:44:00.708
Who the hell is "she"?

698
00:44:03.477 --> 00:44:05.112
(door opens)

699
00:44:05.779 --> 00:44:08.015
(birds chirping)

700
00:44:24.999 --> 00:44:27.001
(phone ringing)

701
00:44:27.468 --> 00:44:29.803
(tense music)
(phone ringing)

702
00:44:46.220 --> 00:44:47.888
(door closes)

703
00:44:52.760 --> 00:44:54.061
(phone ringing)

704
00:44:54.094 --> 00:44:55.829
Who is it?

705
00:44:55.863 --> 00:44:58.432
[Darryl] Well, apparently,

706
00:44:58.465 --> 00:44:59.934
it's Becky.

707
00:45:03.837 --> 00:45:06.340
Went to answer the door
but there was nobody there.

708
00:45:06.373 --> 00:45:08.008
Just this.

709
00:45:08.842 --> 00:45:09.977
Shit.

710
00:45:10.010 --> 00:45:11.145
How the fuck
did she find us?

711
00:45:11.178 --> 00:45:12.213
(coughing)

712
00:45:12.246 --> 00:45:13.480
I'm sorry.

713
00:45:13.515 --> 00:45:15.316
You three know
something about this?

714
00:45:15.349 --> 00:45:17.785
[Anthony] No. Nothing.

715
00:45:17.818 --> 00:45:19.019
One of you care to tell me

716
00:45:19.053 --> 00:45:20.321
what the fuck it is
you're not tellin' me?

717
00:45:20.354 --> 00:45:22.323
-Just tell him, you guys.
-You shut the fuck up.

718
00:45:22.356 --> 00:45:23.791
I think it would be wise

719
00:45:23.824 --> 00:45:25.259
if you listened
to your friend here.

720
00:45:25.292 --> 00:45:26.994
Yeah, what the fuck's
goin' on, gents?

721
00:45:27.027 --> 00:45:28.429
-All right...
-DJ.

722
00:45:28.462 --> 00:45:30.130
All right, fine--no, no,
it's cool, it's cool man.

723
00:45:30.164 --> 00:45:32.066
They're cool, we're gonna just
tell him about the dog, yeah?

724
00:45:32.099 --> 00:45:34.134
-What about the dog?
-[DJ] We took him, that's it.

725
00:45:34.168 --> 00:45:36.070
-[Twig] You took him.
-Yep. Not a big deal.

726
00:45:36.103 --> 00:45:37.371
-Yeah, but that's not it.
-All right.

727
00:45:37.404 --> 00:45:39.039
-Shut the fuck up.
-Shut the fuck up!

728
00:45:39.073 --> 00:45:40.508
All right, all right, fine.

729
00:45:40.542 --> 00:45:42.544
We took him from some
stupid-ass little girl.

730
00:45:42.577 --> 00:45:45.779
That's what Dickless here
wants you to know, okay?

731
00:45:48.215 --> 00:45:49.483
What?

732
00:45:49.517 --> 00:45:50.484
She was fucking with us
at the diner

733
00:45:50.518 --> 00:45:53.153
so we followed her
and stole her fuckin' dog.

734
00:45:53.187 --> 00:45:55.055
Big deal.

735
00:45:55.089 --> 00:45:56.156
Is that what you wanted?

736
00:45:56.190 --> 00:45:57.391
You happy now?

737
00:45:57.858 --> 00:45:59.393
(phone ringing)

738
00:46:00.261 --> 00:46:01.428
Is there any chance that,
that little girl's

739
00:46:01.462 --> 00:46:02.997
name is Becky?

740
00:46:05.600 --> 00:46:07.334
(phone beeps)

741
00:46:08.603 --> 00:46:10.971
[Becky on phone] <i>There</i>
<i>once was a little girl</i>

742
00:46:11.005 --> 00:46:12.973
<i>who had a little curl</i>

743
00:46:13.007 --> 00:46:16.544
